event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":89,"item_id":"rs_0648fac9dcfd996a016aca96a2f8dc819698df31eb3ea02bdc","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering project edits**\n\nI’m looking into how to preserve legacy redirects while managing all priorities through a helper conditional. Should I edit using a script? It seems like I can only edit targeted entries for strings that are unique. It’s confusing because bash replacements are prohibited. I might need to replace entire blocks of unique entries, but I can’t rewrite whole project pages. Maybe focusing on editing entire functions or small blocks could be the way to go."}

